    Question: Harper drinks a 1/2 bottle of mineral water per day. She buys the mineral water by the case at a big box store. They come 24 bottles to a case and are currently on sale for $12.00. If she wants to buy enough cases to last her 240 days, how much will she spend? Think step by step. Answer:Harper drinks a 1/2 bottle of mineral water per day, so she drinks 1/2 * 24 = 12 bottles per day. She wants to buy enough cases to last her 240 days, so she needs to buy 12 bottles per day * 240 days = 2880 bottles. Since there are 24 bottles in a case, she needs to buy 2880 bottles / 24 bottles per case = 120 cases. Since the mineral water is currently on sale for $12.00 per case, Harper will spend 120 cases * $12.00 per case = $1440.00. [...]

